%S A123461 1,2,4,11,33,147,896,8682,131303,3063185,105406803,5159862015,
%T A123461 349345449088
%N A123461 Number of strongly perfect perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123461 A graph is strongly perfect if every induced subgraph has a stable set meeting every maximal clique of that subgraph. The property is hereditary. Disjoint unions and joins of strongly perfect graphs are strongly perfect, and a graph obtained by substituting graphs for the vertices of a quotient graph is strongly perfect if and only if the quotient and all substituted graphs are. The class is not closed under complementation. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 27 2026
%H A123461 S. Hougardy, <a href="https://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
